    description: Archived release of this repository
abstract: >-
  Research code, cleaned corpus and result files for a leakage-free
  two-stage hurdle model of declared building-permit value, built on
  126,837 City of Dallas permit records issued between January 2018 and
  August 2020. The pipeline enforces chronological feature construction
  through point-in-time expanding histories, stage-specific target
  encodings frozen at each evaluation boundary, a 60-day cold-start
  window excluded from model fitting, forward-chaining validation across
  four 2019 quarters, and a single untouched 2020 holdout. Also includes
  the composite permit-type parser audit, naive, log-linear and Tweedie
  comparators, a p99 capping sensitivity analysis, a pre- and
  post-recording-shift evaluation of the classification stage, and a test
  suite verifying the internal consistency of the reported results.
keywords:
  - data leakage
  - temporal validation
  - hurdle model
  - building permits
  - municipal open data
  - urban analytics
  - gradient boosting
  - reproducibility
